OL,3,GNEWSATaoiseach 'not contemplating'
OL,4,Aseparate Omagh bombing inquiry
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe Taoiseach (Irish prime minister)
OL,7,FMicheal Martin has said he is not
OL,8,Fcontemplating a separate public inquiry
OL,9,Finto the Omagh bombing "at the moment".
OL,11,FAmid calls from some victims' relatives
OL,12,Ffor Dublin to commit to its own
OL,13,Finvestigation, Martin said the British
OL,14,Fgovernment's examination must be
OL,15,Fallowed to conclude first.
OL,17,FThe Omagh Bombing Inquiry is
OL,18,Finvestigating whether the attack on 15
OL,19,FAugust 1998, in which 29 people
OL,20,Fincluding a woman pregnant with twins
OL,21,Fwere killed, could have been prevented.
OL,23,APub: 17-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NI NewsC Reg TVF On This Day
FL,414,410,260,120,0,100
